.el .ds Aq '
.TH by 1  "by " 
.SH NAME
by \- List the items that mention `id` — the reverse of `list` — in id order, closed and archived mentioners included. `\-\-type`, `\-\-in` and `\-\-label` narrow it as they narrow `next`; `\-\-limit` shows only the head and says so; `\-\-paginate` adds a token for the next page. Under `\-\-json` the records are `list \-\-json`\*(Aqs, as a plain array — or, with `\-\-limit`, as `{"items": [...], "total": <n>}`, plus `"next_token"` (a string, or null on the last page) and `"restarted"` (bool) with `\-\-paginate`, exactly as `next \-\-limit \-\-json` wraps them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBby\fR [\fB\-\-type\fR] [\fB\-\-in\fR] [\fB\-\-label\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-paginate\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List the items that mention `id` — the reverse of `list` — in id order, closed and archived mentioners included. `\-\-type`, `\-\-in` and `\-\-label` narrow it as they narrow `next`; `\-\-limit` shows only the head and says so; `\-\-paginate` adds a token for the next page. Under `\-\-json` the records are `list \-\-json`\*(Aqs, as a plain array — or, with `\-\-limit`, as `{"items": [...], "total": <n>}`, plus `"next_token"` (a string, or null on the last page) and `"restarted"` (bool) with `\-\-paginate`, exactly as `next \-\-limit \-\-json` wraps them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-type\fR \fI<TYPE>\fR
Only mentioners of this type (the stored type, as `list \-\-type` takes it). Repeatable: the types are alternatives
.TP
\fB\-\-in\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Only mentioners in this container: its children (whose parent it is) and the items that contribute to it
.TP
\fB\-\-label\fR \fI<LABEL>\fR
Only mentioners carrying this label
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR
Max items to show (default: no limit). Applied after the filters and never silently: a truncated list is headed `showing <n> of <total>`, and under `\-\-json` the flag wraps the records as `{"items": [...], "total": <n>}`
.TP
\fB\-\-paginate\fR
Page through the list `\-\-limit` rows at a time: the answer ends with a token for the next page (`next_token` and `restarted` under `\-\-json`). The list is cached on this machine for an hour; a change to an item in it, or a stale or invalid token, restarts at the first page
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
The token a previous `\-\-paginate` answer printed: show the page after that one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The mentioned item
